00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:30,400
Do this whenever you drink it in remembrance of me.

692
00:40:30,400 --> 00:40:32,500
For whenever you eat this bread and drink this cup,

693
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:34,860
you proclaim the Lord's death until he comes.

694
00:40:41,540 --> 00:40:50,220
Lord Father God, thank you this morning for what you've given us.

695
00:40:50,220 --> 00:40:54,800
The opportunities that you've given us to share others.

696
00:40:54,800 --> 00:41:01,820
The responsibilities you've given us from which we can learn a tiniest slip of what it's like to be you.

697
00:41:01,820 --> 00:41:04,240
To take care of others made in your image.

698
00:41:05,920 --> 00:41:08,800
For those this morning that struggle from hand to mouth.

699
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:13,980
That struggle to take care of multiple children on a shoestring budget.

700
00:41:13,980 --> 00:41:17,640
I pray that you would help them find the joy in your provision for them.

701
00:41:17,640 --> 00:41:21,280
And a release from the strain and the fear of tomorrow.

702
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:29,200
And for those of us who have put so much effort into trying to build for tomorrow.

703
00:41:29,200 --> 00:41:31,900
That it's become a fixation for us.

704
00:41:31,900 --> 00:41:34,980
I pray that you would help us find the joy of your provision.

705
00:41:35,200 --> 00:41:38,420
And let go of our pride in which we believe we've done for ourselves.

706
00:41:38,420 --> 00:41:42,380
And that you would help us see the value in those around us.

707
00:41:42,380 --> 00:41:44,420
Including our own family.

708
00:41:44,420 --> 00:41:47,740
The value they have before your kingdom.

709
00:41:47,740 --> 00:41:50,000
As part of your design.

710
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:53,480
And that we would seek first the kingdom of God and your righteousness.

711
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:57,460
So that all the other things that we need will be added to us by your gracious kindness.

712
00:41:57,460 --> 00:41:59,240
And we would recognize it for that when it happens.

713
00:41:59,240 --> 00:42:01,660
Thank you.

714
00:42:01,660 --> 00:42:03,660
In Jesus name.

715
00:42:03,660 --> 00:42:04,100
Amen.

716
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:11,200
So may the peace of God which us surpasses all understanding guard your hearts and minds in Christ Jesus.

717
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:14,020
Go with God and we'll see you here next week.

718
00:42:14,020 --> 00:42:14,820
Thank you very much.

719
00:42:23,700 --> 00:42:33,320
I don't know what it's like to be.

720
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:34,640
I don't know what it's like to be you.

721
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:39,700
You don't know what it's like to be me.

722
00:42:39,700 --> 00:42:46,560
What if we're all the same in different kinds of ways.

723
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:48,760
Can you, can you relate?

724
00:42:49,160 --> 00:43:15,320
Have you ever been left when you should have been loved?

725
00:43:16,780 --> 00:43:20,360
Has there ever been a time when you stayed but you should have run?

726
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:22,800
Cause I've been real, I've been faking.

727
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:27,520
Been a sinner, been a saint.

728
00:43:27,520 --> 00:43:33,620
I've been right, I've been so, so wrong.

729
00:43:33,620 --> 00:43:36,680
Yeah, I've made my mistakes.

730
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:39,440
Now I don't know what it's like to be you.

731
00:43:39,440 --> 00:43:44,460
You don't know what it's like to be me.

732
00:43:44,460 --> 00:43:45,840
I don't know what it's like to be me.
